    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The mass of a radioactive substance in grams is given by $M=80e^{-0.021t}$ where $t$ is in years. Find the mass after 15 years, rounding to 2 d.p. Then state what the mass becomes as $t\\to\\infty$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$58.38\\text{ g}$; the mass approaches $0\\text{ g}$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}M(15)&=80e^{-0.021(15)}\\\\M(15)&=80e^{-0.315}\\\\M(15)&\\approx58.38\\text{ g}\\end{align*}$$\nAs $t\\to\\infty$, $e^{-0.021t}\\to0$, so $M\\to0\\text{ g}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
